---
// The "random note" link beside the search button, in both the mobile navbar
// and the sidebar (`NavShell.astro`). It goes to `/random/`, which sends the
// reader to a note picked at random (`pages/random.astro`). Live had no such
// link; the page existed, but nothing pointed to it (docs/design-changes.md).
//
// It is a link, not a button like search: it navigates, so it is an `<a>`
// that opens in a new tab or copies like any other link, and it works without
// JavaScript (search is hidden then; this is not). The icon is decoration;
// `aria-label` names the link for screen readers and `title` gives pointer
// users a tooltip, since the link has no visible text.
//
// Styling (ADR 0003 phase 2): the same 36px box as the search button, so the
// two read as a pair on one row; the row itself (the gap, who grows) is
// NavShell's. The color is inherited, as the search button's is: the
// sidebar's muted gray there and the body text color in the navbar. Keyboard
// focus uses the global ring in styles/base.css.
import Icon from "./Icon.astro";
---

<a
  href="/random/"
  class="my-2.5 flex size-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-gray-700 bg-gray-950 text-inherit hover:border-gray-100"
  aria-label="Random note"
  title="Random note"
>
  <Icon name="dices" class="pointer-events-none size-3.5 opacity-70" />
</a>
